3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Breman</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The ears of the hippopotamus: Manifestations, determinants and estimates of the malaria burden</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><year>2001</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11504397</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Abdalla</surname><given-names>SIA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The national burden of selected diseases and injuries in Sudan in 2002</article-title><source>MD thesis</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>University of Khartoum, Community Medicine Department</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>WHO health statistics and health information systems. Deaths and DALY estimates for 2002 by cause for WHO member states</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/healthinfo/statistics/bodgbddeathdalyestimates.xls"/></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Snow</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Craig</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Deichmann</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Marsh</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Estimating mortality, morbidity and disability due to malaria among Africa's non-pregnant population</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><year>1999</year><volume>77</volume><fpage>624</fpage><lpage>640</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10516785</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kruijshaar</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Barendregt</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoeymans</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The use of models in the estimation of disease epidemiology</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><year>2002</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>622</fpage><lpage>628</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12219152</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>MARA/ARMA project. Seasonality of malaria transmission in Sudan</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.mara.org.za/pdfmaps/SudSeasonality.PDF"/></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>